#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc27e22-d687-533a-9a5a-f8ec0e2b1bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354793} {:answer/id #uuid "85ca94ec-7195-5aa1-bbbd-cc72022d704a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355843} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a1b26f-a343-5137-9997-11acffc2bef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356115} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe1bea9-6907-59a2-b366-e66cbf9da2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356443} {:answer/id #uuid "fa70dd31-26d4-5dea-9543-934d2d9ce29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356854}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186356854} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bae90e8-c7ce-52ff-a590-5fbc1f33fd7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9f5a627e-5fd5-5321-b04e-df13a3c56af4" :question/math-academy-id "q-91229" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & -6\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-6-5) \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357515 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a477994-9c45-55b2-8144-b3659d076ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355191} {:answer/id #uuid "53f32427-b796-5beb-a84b-c128fa08761b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355410} {:answer/id #uuid "54c31c85-f366-5772-9219-7e9652a6a9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355416} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5679cc-5df2-5e8d-be56-472423bde4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355613} {:answer/id #uuid "fb93e011-84ae-5f31-935d-2c2555d5038d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356861}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355191} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee71f6d-313c-5faf-9cbb-6d25c54df71c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "15878489-f600-5d8d-a45e-e1a6680dcacf" :question/math-academy-id "q-91232" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(49-25) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc7bfb2-2de4-5825-9ad1-7d1cca5c1673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357864} {:answer/id #uuid "2e119460-b615-5584-b834-96ed6a634d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=1,\\,b=6,\\,c=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358166} {:answer/id #uuid "40f48421-b4d5-510e-a696-56a31fba8676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358302} {:answer/id #uuid "4b96e53e-09ae-5fec-8b1d-15b0b47f2745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358403} {:answer/id #uuid "601832e1-0bd0-529a-9f76-558c73116ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358592}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358403} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee2810a-7014-5a58-9251-1f7a6f92a507" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b4913b2d-3ba5-5e48-86c0-076ebc0464a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-9720" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x &=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z &=2 \\\\ x+3z-y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 3x+6y-2z &=2 \\\\ x-y+3z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ac7900-ea05-5cc8-9d53-11c30c4ca60a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440029} {:answer/id #uuid "91747f90-b1ca-5a23-b764-3011370995c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440030}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440029} :answer-field/id #uuid "536c4571-b3d8-5ac6-b419-3f6f71056077" :answer-field/key "$k=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1e4cb25-b3e5-5104-8ec6-1f86c12d56d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440031} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff679bc-fdfb-5669-bd8b-854d2358190c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440032}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440032} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c431c2-1fb0-5a03-b48d-74276cb322b4" :answer-field/key "$k=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9399f58c-b270-5d89-8f0f-c6e1b2ae15a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440033} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd73f80-9ac4-5715-aa47-0376b208e6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440034} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7c8be4f-cbe0-55fc-a506-530979c94394" :answer-field/key "$k=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e554c090-e3bc-5a93-90b4-9f79a0997b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-9911" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}k & -k \\\\ k & k\\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{vmatrix}+k\\begin{vmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =({k}^{2}+{k}^{2})+(k+5k)+k(k-5k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k+k\\cdot (-4k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-4{k}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{k}^{2}+6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{k}^{2}+6k & =0 \\\\ k(-2k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=0$ and $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28576cc0-5b53-52a1-993c-52e6981f0e23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361011} {:answer/id #uuid "41df7ae9-3272-5a1d-b2c6-8730c296899a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "Any real number" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361129} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b997e7-f26c-5ca5-b635-2f16f0cab1c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361556} {:answer/id #uuid "a555d756-093c-5a66-ac31-9396b628afff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361577} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a9bece-ac6f-57f6-abed-e01a47669f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361800}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186361556} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3d836f-c871-5036-ada8-8e641e2d9862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ec95474f-3d89-5428-8221-da33b63b3f3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9961" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ is $-6$, find the value of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =4-n\\cdot 2+0 \\\\  & =4-2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-6,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2n & =-6 \\\\ -2n & =-10 \\\\ n & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fdc5b0e-70ba-55cb-b45b-203a37baf9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363082} {:answer/id #uuid "da61ad95-87fa-55dc-a753-f99e1006fa25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363083} {:answer/id #uuid "b84e370b-eb8b-5320-a8cc-dbe74b5db419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363084} {:answer/id #uuid "aa206ae0-5d13-50d6-abe7-71da4033c4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363085} {:answer/id #uuid "899b2eaf-81cc-5d6d-8850-eccd2284315a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363086}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363082} :answer-field/id #uuid "59f088e4-8267-5e3a-8395-4af841304036" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a7ba9088-1a5a-5dc8-89fa-4feea7488ee8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131498" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+5y+0z &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n-x+5y=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=5y-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5y-3 \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5y-3 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aae47a05-fe93-5f17-98f6-16fc7f0340ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363089} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7f75fa-ad4a-542b-9dea-7a2105243786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363090} {:answer/id #uuid "6c588b82-80a1-5c78-9100-d60a55699a98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363091} {:answer/id #uuid "c02a65d7-eb58-572e-89ef-44df7dceaf04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363092} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb6f524-83ed-59cb-9fd9-092153a63286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363093}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363089} :answer-field/id #uuid "f05dbd06-439c-5d04-a158-7e565bd03228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bfa7ac48-5370-571f-9289-0bc53c057572" :question/math-academy-id "q-131503" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-15{x}_{3} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & -15 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & -15 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -5 & -15 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4b2e2b5-5692-5b4a-804f-7518ab214d08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437872} {:answer/id #uuid "3acb46da-0035-5f87-8672-6682f18cf559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437873}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437873} :answer-field/id #uuid "477f40a4-66af-5870-95c1-78ba941c5598" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438965} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7886ec-2b7c-5184-ba5d-a9cfd3f447ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437874} {:answer/id #uuid "1b86766c-211b-5526-8849-1753bc7e2812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437875}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437874} :answer-field/id #uuid "76f4b7f4-de99-5ebc-a3fb-5f5fcbe4139b" :answer-field/key "The system has no solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d52184b-23ff-5d3d-be0f-8e48b9e54a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437876} {:answer/id #uuid "545708f8-29e7-5393-a590-6497da645a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437876} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b08613c-08bd-5a65-b4c6-d5cae5341709" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "230d301d-cd52-59f0-8164-f9d6e6d6aa03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669033} {:answer/id #uuid "15fe0392-248f-5ff4-a855-b9b2944ddc6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186669033} :answer-field/id #uuid "f97dadb8-fd7f-558c-945b-4c4b5badb293" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186669316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e8de2435-5f56-5017-bf79-0b535c719854" :question/math-academy-id "q-131718" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=2 \\\\ -2x+7y+2z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent dependent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d434ad9-8516-5f67-a1c8-b8fb37dbe476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3-4y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364346} {:answer/id #uuid "e3736c0c-8456-559a-8dcc-35d30f71662a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y-4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364347} {:answer/id #uuid "0ddbfea5-412d-5c3e-9b96-6f20638d2e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-3y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364348} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6f3510-c082-55c3-bfcc-e61d7d386624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364349} {:answer/id #uuid "c8dd9ac2-9ed3-5fe2-b588-e1515f753cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364350}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364350} :answer-field/id #uuid "9615cffd-ab8b-596e-89a9-eab03c7aa9d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5f569855-d257-5ea3-9d07-8247dc046d5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-73914" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 12 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -8 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-4z &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx+2y-4z=3\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=3-2y+4z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-2y+4z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y+4z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e2d5a83-8718-5bdf-8eb3-db892e2ab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} {:answer/id #uuid "8eaaea36-3739-5e8a-a1ed-efc15f9bc00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438533}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438532} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efd7542-c77b-5d4d-8f60-5468e0925423" :answer-field/key "The system has no solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439295} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "763f0363-fe65-5380-acc8-6965de771643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438534} {:answer/id #uuid "be014b12-0b58-51d7-a7a3-d343e4554293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438535} :answer-field/id #uuid "1338d41d-dfae-54bb-ada6-b58b1d8cc303" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439296} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48fb77e-36ef-5915-aaab-7df2660d984a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} {:answer/id #uuid "84b40478-f69c-539e-aac5-dd183a05b951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438537}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438536} :answer-field/id #uuid "7051a40c-c2de-5375-95a6-8801b39f67c5" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "35b0295d-1e16-59cc-a201-696e791e0b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74643" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=8 \\\\ x+y &=-2 \\\\ x+\\frac{1}{2}y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=-2 \\\\ -y &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b194044-2804-5fcf-a8b9-85153f639110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364950} {:answer/id #uuid "54638e37-8e75-56d4-9a53-7e2c86da678b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364951} {:answer/id #uuid "c81acd3d-ac95-59d4-82b7-c347ecf84382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364952} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9c5b60-f770-5f9a-ba14-7c25357899e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364953} {:answer/id #uuid "00b39530-0e0b-51c1-a111-9de7ad7bbe3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364954}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364953} :answer-field/id #uuid "edaea1a1-bae4-5261-82aa-d4974642b5d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "16690ec9-e7e6-5efe-838c-d6c519315582" :question/math-academy-id "q-128308" :question/problem "Find the value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =7\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =7(6-1)-1(0+3)-3(0+9) \\\\  & =7\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =35-3-27 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e1e46e-bc20-5e49-8f3c-e2b13ee9e67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{67}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365549} :answer-field/id #uuid "20261a72-2d87-53f3-be96-928a95530e46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fbb701de-fecd-5033-b2e0-5f19c68c7b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280402" :question/problem "Given that $B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & k+2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $det(B)=70$, find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & k+2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{vmatrix}k+2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & k+2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(6\\cdot (k+2)-(-5)(-1))+2(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (k+2)) \\\\  & =3(6k+12-5)+2(-1-4k-8) \\\\  & =3(6k+7)+2(-4k-9) \\\\  & =18k+21-8k-18 \\\\  & =10k+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $70,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10k+3 & =70 \\\\ 10k & =67 \\\\ k & =\\frac{67}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e337463-b3e6-57c5-a2b0-3b2f8be1327c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365552}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365552} :answer-field/id #uuid "113f8edf-ce63-5e3c-8e20-25df8fcc000b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5aa7c3b-3cc6-5915-9f4e-4ad87619a68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365554}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365554} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae0cbef-0d94-5f00-b36b-22a479b003a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7046d61a-2100-5f6e-80e3-9459516462dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-280543" :question/problem "Find, in **ascending order**, the values ​​of $x$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}x+2 & 2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & x & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{vmatrix}x+2 & 2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & x & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & =(x+2)\\begin{vmatrix}x & x+1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2x\\begin{vmatrix}3 & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+4\\begin{vmatrix}3 & x \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(x+2)(3x)-2x(8-x)+4(-x) \\\\  & =3x(x+2)-2x(8-x)-4x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+6x-16x+2{x}^{2}-4x \\\\  & =5{x}^{2}-14x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-14x & =0 \\\\ x(5x-14) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{14}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c502c08e-cbb1-5442-bcb9-424b6777ac3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438664} {:answer/id #uuid "003139e8-881a-52b3-9ea9-221baca3d942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438665}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438664} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee174a06-895c-5583-812c-7c4468fa2511" :answer-field/key "$det(D)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4493f073-130a-5643-b440-425f3034460d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438666} {:answer/id #uuid "0508c95e-9b72-5cb3-8464-ae610809503a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438667} :answer-field/id #uuid "495bc1a5-e85e-5043-b4d4-3fe8b15554ed" :answer-field/key "$D$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439362} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1502369-e88d-503e-90f4-0f6ab218c61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438668} {:answer/id #uuid "516ece6f-6106-541c-abfc-8c583469231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438669}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186438669} :answer-field/id #uuid "e222facc-8617-59fb-b0f3-b2ffe6c181c7" :answer-field/key "$det(D)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e3acb77-06f5-5592-8e02-3140d23a412e" :question/math-academy-id "q-9835" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $D$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(28-30)-2(7-5)+3(6-4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-2-4+6 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(D)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements “$D$ is a singular matrix” and $det(D)=0$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3033aa1-cb1b-51d7-bd66-84b07ac416e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375918} {:answer/id #uuid "0864e58a-33de-52c4-a01e-09b896904513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375919} {:answer/id #uuid "38d0d5d6-e7f8-51b0-a5c1-d9f6154b91c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375920} {:answer/id #uuid "27092bc7-551b-5545-b710-7b71ed7f703f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375921} {:answer/id #uuid "b642da4d-bd4e-52d0-9efc-082398abd7df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375919} :answer-field/id #uuid "730549d1-5dd7-5d03-a4f9-dc98698c3514" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b7ea406-9f82-5933-b31e-095d9f01e027" :question/math-academy-id "q-130646" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${C}^{2}=C,$ so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.  \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{4} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot {C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & ={C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{C}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce3c5f0-7529-5c2c-9564-44c889eb86c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0a7954-cd05-51a7-90b9-b780bf965f6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453387}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453386} :answer-field/id #uuid "bca78a15-c48c-5741-abab-0bf7b97a57a4" :answer-field/key "The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcec78e2-d6bb-56c4-ad75-975ad764b8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} {:answer/id #uuid "292a5262-ac7c-5df9-a70a-6d1d92a3b30d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453389}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd94f480-acd9-57b8-a0ef-b55824c69c2f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd8e82d-abc1-543c-9e38-eb7d06e6eeb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453390} {:answer/id #uuid "399ad536-9e21-50bb-b29b-6a5685869bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453391} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcdeb836-29c1-560f-b756-552781011c7f" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8048be79-9af8-51c0-a0c1-5b68f549139c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139986" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=4=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “The number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $3$” is false. Since the generating vectors in \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\nare linearly independent, we conclude that the number of non-pivot columns in $A$ is equal to $1.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=1\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=4.$ Now, according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9290da55-a6a3-5bb8-a9b8-2039b243ee6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453404} {:answer/id #uuid "adeaa133-0730-51b1-8b37-ab1eabd66c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453405} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f82a48-c4e0-5658-a295-60736c7e5166" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88d7d24f-3606-50eb-9098-a34319240958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} {:answer/id #uuid "535a174d-2f6e-5ab0-99bb-3ccad768cc35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453406} :answer-field/id #uuid "59aa5f02-f270-5643-aeca-3ee7824a7629" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99558d31-6961-52e7-b662-299510c283b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} {:answer/id #uuid "688a37cc-bcaf-529c-a80d-90d43dc9aa3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453409}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186453408} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f387ba8-880e-5912-8b03-6a51150d10c2" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "017db163-2592-561e-a975-d762dc265a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-142542" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\text{Span}\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$\n\n \nwe have that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nNow,  for the matrix $A,$ the number of columns is $n=5,$ so according to the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(A)=2\\ne 0,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  invertible” is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3\\ne 5$, according to the  invertible matrix theorem $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1ec707-d108-5c5f-95b9-f01b95149735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377737} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceb5c0a-088d-5afe-9529-7e677309be1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377738} {:answer/id #uuid "16377926-6078-5e5e-8a56-d2bb1659e827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377739} {:answer/id #uuid "1d542b8a-f667-583d-8708-e581bf10d752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377740} {:answer/id #uuid "558c0201-332f-5cb3-b439-ba474404267a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377741}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377740} :answer-field/id #uuid "d57be3b3-e112-57f7-b6a6-16bbac625c72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "07ba9ea7-a44e-52e4-bff2-32246bba4f40" :question/math-academy-id "q-78576" :question/problem "If $U=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${U}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${U}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${U}^{2}=U,$ so $U$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${U}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & ={U}^{2} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{U}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca86402-c665-55ad-96e2-e7faee870cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377758} {:answer/id #uuid "701ec281-64bf-55a9-a13a-9af209eaff5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377759} {:answer/id #uuid "93249bda-5da5-5cfd-8d15-56c91976394d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377760} {:answer/id #uuid "60b2f467-bf50-5ae6-993c-21e4a93659ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377761} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdd441a-d8f0-5c12-b7bc-0bc161b02d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377760} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef6c019-6203-53f2-a536-cc2b8d76a9fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0131f756-450c-5ffd-bd43-d0c24b54342a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79352" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $$\n\\displaystyle \\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee3ba979-73eb-55d9-98be-53eb63f15310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454018} {:answer/id #uuid "42f7e70e-a33c-5389-83b8-4b66c4b40413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454019} :answer-field/id #uuid "51beb1c0-c434-5ffe-be4f-d1af3a966f94" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b27c5d69-4610-55e4-befd-bab1f9f21b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454020} {:answer/id #uuid "7f38039b-9493-5449-afe0-51512728ff71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454021} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd2f4dc-0220-560a-b969-e0fb63f01a28" :answer-field/key "$A$ is not  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22168706-fdd0-5ec9-8357-a478a254b0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} {:answer/id #uuid "b3eaef39-5ed2-5d0e-8448-e5d92a445686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454023}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186454022} :answer-field/id #uuid "447c453c-9c02-53db-ad8b-23d0593303f4" :answer-field/key "$\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c7ff497-8845-5d34-a5a1-e0b10d7a1e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-79367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)=3$ is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is not  invertible” is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$ is false. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=3$; “$A$ is not  invertible” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd0c887f-bc11-51df-8072-17fb96605fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378645} {:answer/id #uuid "51e2abb9-8c36-55cf-8b11-5be5cc04d4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}200 & 100 \\\\ 400 & 200\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378646} {:answer/id #uuid "910da761-c886-5a47-82cb-314cbf3244c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}200 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 200\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378647} {:answer/id #uuid "a3ccd3c9-da6d-587a-8df0-2e6a05b497cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}75 & 75 \\\\ 150 & 150\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378648} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9d2198-a4da-5b98-b875-712f22b11289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}125 & 100 \\\\ 100 & 125\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378645} :answer-field/id #uuid "34ee98b2-1184-57a5-866e-b115787035a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fec19e3b-a382-541e-8dfb-bf5969fae1bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130618" :question/problem "If $S=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 \\\\ -20 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${S}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${S}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{2} & =S\\cdot S \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 \\\\ -20 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}10 & 5 \\\\ -20 & -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${S}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $S$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${S}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{3} & ={S}^{2}\\cdot S \\\\  & =O\\cdot S \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{S}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79b2bcf4-f46d-55ce-953b-d5aab772f415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}60 & 50 \\\\ 50 & 60\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378652} {:answer/id #uuid "f8deafff-c5ea-5241-b228-7dc8e2c7175d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378653} {:answer/id #uuid "4e38bc9e-f5e7-54ea-9030-8112e36dece2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}150 & 250 \\\\ 90 & 150\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378654} {:answer/id #uuid "7dea9004-2a5e-5c5f-b23c-a74a5363695e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & -9 \\\\ 15 & -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378655} {:answer/id #uuid "35b46246-26d9-5b02-b5fa-4340136d55f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378656}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378653} :answer-field/id #uuid "c733bd9e-c4fb-53e2-949a-5c503e09863d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b3acafe4-9ff1-5be0-a11c-248c3e1c6303" :question/math-academy-id "q-130622" :question/problem "If $R=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 25 \\\\ -9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${R}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2} & =R\\cdot R \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 25 \\\\ -9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 25 \\\\ -9 & 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${R}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $R$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${R}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2} & ={R}^{2}\\cdot {R}^{2} \\\\  & =O\\cdot O \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{R}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486cf915-4729-5348-a631-1139c564eaa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379374} {:answer/id #uuid "7e9c83be-9f24-5f3f-a844-8cd7595ce2a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379375} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b76ef5-d10d-55c7-a887-ad88a55019ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379376} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f49551-908e-5122-852e-5f3eff7e718e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379377} {:answer/id #uuid "144b697a-2f51-540f-8ade-3378764bdab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379378} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f5ddba-5ada-5bb1-a40b-00deae59b918" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "44f0704d-d888-58ac-9a01-4ee289c5ce3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-32425" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${C}^{2}=C,$ so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{3} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot C \\\\  & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & ={C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6905e492-1bfa-56e9-96f6-b16f42f18195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379381} {:answer/id #uuid "23599c7f-a156-5ca4-a4c0-6bb5286b6542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379382} {:answer/id #uuid "dd401fd4-56d3-5cd5-b282-79caa53da359" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379383} {:answer/id #uuid "493397d8-4b69-55ab-92fe-895e0b84d275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379384} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0f1c5b-31d9-570b-96cb-f2a70d1062be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379383} :answer-field/id #uuid "a45d61de-6617-5713-b9a5-59e4fc821552" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "94b8854f-eadf-5679-a6d5-099961aad0a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-32427" :question/problem "If $$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$ then ${B}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${B}^{2}=B,$ so $B$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${B}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{4} & ={B}^{2}\\cdot {B}^{2} \\\\  & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & ={B}^{2} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{B}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cb7ce1a-60a1-5128-a371-0a24aee8aaaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380092} {:answer/id #uuid "183e4c93-edef-530c-9b88-03e531d149b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380093} {:answer/id #uuid "119f20f7-c59d-5da7-b926-9f3fb348e455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380094} {:answer/id #uuid "a2204f3b-10a6-5002-b291-3d611ba4d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380095} {:answer/id #uuid "57a7a319-9c32-5c85-aae9-9b79769bf680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380096}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380093} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d7e7d8-b930-5a83-889f-a4b032dfb56c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "26013839-bad8-5e18-94c9-d8c0f29f855d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78573" :question/problem "If $V=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${V}^{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${V}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{2} & =V\\cdot V \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${V}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $V$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${V}^{7}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{7} & ={V}^{2}\\cdot {V}^{5} \\\\  & =O\\cdot {V}^{5} \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{V}^{7}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98256a85-e8bc-5140-b031-8d97dad3a8c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380099} {:answer/id #uuid "d757ba88-edcb-54bc-a513-21902b3eda6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380100} {:answer/id #uuid "375fd459-c1a3-5977-9b9d-89dd8874308d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380101} {:answer/id #uuid "178aa65c-5124-50e4-8822-83db1352c41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380102} {:answer/id #uuid "531d1c12-7af4-5a74-a0d7-40bddf5a6645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380103}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380100} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2aa84bf-fb35-5eec-b119-c07a40b91542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380098}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d7861f5f-5e43-5ff5-8123-034b760f1322" :question/math-academy-id "q-78574" :question/problem "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${P}^{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${P}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{2} & =P\\cdot P \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${P}^{2}=P,$ so $P$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${P}^{6}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{6} & ={P}^{2}\\cdot {P}^{2}\\cdot {P}^{2} \\\\  & =P\\cdot P\\cdot P \\\\  & ={P}^{2}\\cdot P \\\\  & =P\\cdot P \\\\  & ={P}^{2} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{P}^{6}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "752f25aa-4fc1-51e6-a013-9b80e8827572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380917} {:answer/id #uuid "5f33c54b-5751-550c-80ee-312c7a25a862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380918} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1a5bfb-1813-5146-9082-83c4984a5e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380919} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca9b5d9-6498-5036-89e7-97ff59128a90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380920} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd4bf4a-5003-57f0-8acd-836bc85a56e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380921}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380917} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7062c0-01e1-52e1-8ed5-92b3891749a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380916}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca4ecbae-990a-5f1f-aeca-c9cba7c7191b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131501" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y-5z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx+3y-5z=1\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=1-3y+5z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1-3y+5z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+y\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1708af3-801d-584a-aeda-c6af402ec801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388120} {:answer/id #uuid "40cbdb8f-877f-53aa-bf79-d36f72cd4d55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388121} {:answer/id #uuid "e11459e8-1503-5456-9678-aba1dd86d574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388122} {:answer/id #uuid "ef918f37-4863-551b-85f0-0ef99235420c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -64 \\\\ 1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388123} {:answer/id #uuid "67d2bb18-e796-50b7-84e1-c25a426ff8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388124}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388121} :answer-field/id #uuid "e97cb90a-b2dc-5df1-adaf-1eeeb866d705" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d89d4cfc-04ae-58b4-94a3-0a7fbe7e0bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130591" :question/problem "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${B}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${B}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${B}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $B$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${B}^{3}$ quickly, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{3} & ={B}^{2}\\cdot B \\\\  & =O\\cdot B \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  \n\n$$\n{B}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e627bf06-b7ea-50b3-acce-c3329b78924d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 \\\\ -16 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388127} {:answer/id #uuid "5c21fb6e-803b-5e13-a8cb-6304943f7142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388128} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb92062-e269-5103-bcb6-ee423244fa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}36 & 16 \\\\ -81 & -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388129} {:answer/id #uuid "3315e19a-b288-5c35-a34c-9df664109377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 24 \\\\ 36 & -24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388130} {:answer/id #uuid "a7284b09-01f1-5a6d-ad9a-2ea872545748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}32 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -32\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388131}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388128} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd0d8c1-ad3e-559b-a9bd-7b4bb6172f7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce36ac4d-8289-51ae-b2d5-2c062b43f9e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130606" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${C}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ -9 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${C}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $C$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot {C}^{2} \\\\  & =O\\cdot O \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{C}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3918d02d-79a2-5245-9ab6-bd95e4e96915" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388253} {:answer/id #uuid "2c45615d-4f2b-5ac9-b5dc-e4f43dac6ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 3\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388254} {:answer/id #uuid "36c6b408-d5d5-589a-a660-9ef15feecae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388255} {:answer/id #uuid "58472625-1fbc-537b-9c8f-5e2f7ee28d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 9 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388256} {:answer/id #uuid "7d18a2b2-9593-54ad-b487-9d6b01810ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388257}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388255} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ab624e-b5cd-5b5e-8dbf-171c60613d15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "16ee071c-dc61-52a6-97dd-99854448ee3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-132003" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f5b753a-7fbd-50d8-93d7-41cd57d255eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388864} {:answer/id #uuid "1126107e-186e-5040-9398-edb4d6acbbee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388865} {:answer/id #uuid "387d733c-7cfe-5c37-a088-20da0dfb5afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388866} {:answer/id #uuid "65011359-a368-5adf-95bc-7e28380bf0fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388867} {:answer/id #uuid "e576812b-f2a8-5232-87cf-c83d5c6c9f02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388868}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388864} :answer-field/id #uuid "c07f5031-bde3-5457-acc7-6e1f7faa31d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4a3cbd65-d830-59dc-8511-5f72908033d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-142485" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $4\\times 5$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $2$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-2 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51ba5d1d-917f-578b-b236-84c5ce425052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390752} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbe959f-5587-55cc-8bae-e699339e8f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390753} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7a779e-0566-5402-a151-8dcb0f8c03e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390754} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea01b22-3015-5978-9cd8-0f6cd3a74b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390755} {:answer/id #uuid "ded05c43-29b2-5aa4-ac03-348898ec9d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390756}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390755} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec20b706-5b72-5579-8d68-048b9d6753ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a7c08cd8-33d8-5be3-943c-1859738a0181" :question/math-academy-id "q-32436" :question/problem "If \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${D}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${D}^{2}=D,$ so $D$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${D}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{3} & ={D}^{2}\\cdot D \\\\  & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & ={D}^{2} \\\\  & =D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{D}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d15d9f3-732b-55fc-82a8-ea78dc52e1fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391960} {:answer/id #uuid "62095833-a3c7-56bd-8dae-b6e79ea4ea2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391961} {:answer/id #uuid "57d7afe0-ca6f-57d3-a2e3-906ad22f4aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391962} {:answer/id #uuid "37bb6378-9f91-5ead-9cda-c102778d5f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391963} {:answer/id #uuid "9580bf69-88fc-535e-8e59-7eee0bdecc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391964}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391961} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e7b743d-c43a-510a-a794-32f1c29c8d88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2594c879-7fd1-5b85-9df5-7ae761ff92cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-36302" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${C}^{2}=C,$ so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{3} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot C \\\\  & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & ={C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{C}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d35eed70-a904-57c6-8b36-1d024048da1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392130} {:answer/id #uuid "324311ee-397f-5fcf-8380-cacd9ae6d35d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392131} {:answer/id #uuid "a325f15c-6e90-5bde-9158-27dc61018674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392132} {:answer/id #uuid "b3156e84-9b52-5f08-a0d8-db8b8472491c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392133} {:answer/id #uuid "02b183e3-094a-5114-879b-f7cae7db166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392134}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392133} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c57e752-231d-5c0a-9ac8-edbce417ffee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7bafb401-a99c-58a5-8622-a9ebf82083bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-37649" :question/problem "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a13c92c1-d46b-5ad3-8d49-d657ae852b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392530} {:answer/id #uuid "811f866b-ae8b-5db0-8fdc-3c3f50d0a8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392531} {:answer/id #uuid "68926b34-a3f3-5a47-9fe2-1458dd7215a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392532} {:answer/id #uuid "e277425a-ae05-5bac-a970-b87c4dbd71f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392533} {:answer/id #uuid "b24ea19e-100f-52b8-974f-8dda2d79d59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392534}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392533} :answer-field/id #uuid "98a2e875-16b0-58cc-98c8-26e2d0c18d89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "76b3cd6b-fbb2-5a67-a041-718320a952b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-42902" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 4\\end{vmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
